<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n287" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαλλι-άω</span></b> , late form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγάλλομαι,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rejoice exceedingly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Apoc.
				19.7
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαλλιώμεθα</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; ἠγαλλίᾱσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
					1.47
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1592.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii/iv A.D.)</span>:—more common as Dep.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαλλιάομαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Is.</u>
				12.6
			</span></i>, al.: fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ps.</u>
					5.11
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγαλλιᾱσάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ps.</u>
					15(16).2
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Jo.</u>
				8.56
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγαλλιάσθην</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.35
			</span></i>.—This family of words seems also to have been used
				<i>in malam partem,</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
